# =============================================================================
#  .gitignore: Multilingual Audio Red-Teaming of Gemma 4
#  Commit code, prompt sets, docs and each run's results/settings.
#  Keep secrets, generated audio, logs and machine-specific files out.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Real API keys. Each person copies .env.example to .env.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Runs: commit results + settings, not bulky or temporary files ----------
# Kept:    runs/<name>_run/run_info.json, dataset.json, results.json
# Ignored: the audio (about 0.5-1 GB per full run) and detailed batch logs.
#          To share audio, use the shared Drive folder (README section 9),
#          or delete the "audio/" line below if you use Git LFS.
experiments/runs/*/audio/
experiments/runs/*/logs/
experiments/runs/*/.lock
experiments/runs/*/latest.json

# Atomic-write temp files (left behind only if a save is interrupted)
*.tmp

# --- Legacy outputs (--id/--all without --run) -------------------------------
experiments/audio_standard/
experiments/audio/
experiments/latest_ultimate.json

# --- Audio anywhere else (archive clips, one-off tests) ----------------------
*.wav
*.mp3

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/

# --- Archive -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Outdated material from earlier versions; not part of the current workflow.
# Kept on disk / in the shared Drive for reference, never committed.
_archive/

# --- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
